WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.230
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and hopefully
you’ve had a chance to see the Book 3 finale.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:11.360
Because it’s two episodes together I’m
going to make this a top 10 video. I know

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.170
a lot of you still have big questions about
Book 4 with all the changes and the show moving

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:21.570
to digital only. Don’t worry, they’re
finishing book 4 and it will also be all digital.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.310
No official release date yet. But plan for
next summer until we hear otherwise.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.300
I’ll explain what kind of Avatar and Korra
videos I’m doing now that the season is

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.080
over. But the giveaway will still run for
another week. All you have to do to enter

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.109
is be a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:38.109
Here we go, TOP 10 moments from the Korra
finale, careful for spoilers in case you haven’t

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.329
seen it yet. I’ll wait just a sec….Here
We go.

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:48.910
Number 10 - Korra decides to give herself
up

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:52.440
There were a lot of Last Airbender parallels
with the way the finale went down. Korra making

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.840
the hard choice to turn herself in really
reminded me of Sozin’s Comet Part 2 where

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.539
Aang had run off to meditate and came to the
conclusion he would have to kill Ozai which

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:03.789
was completely against all of his beliefs
as an airbender.

00:01:03.789 --> 00:01:09.720
Korra makes the choice with no assurance she’ll
survive. I like that they made that clear.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:15.340
She’s the gung-ho avatar, which is like
the polar opposite of Aang who was the reluctant

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:15.860
Avatar. So she’s just going to leave it
up to her friends to rescue her in an attempt

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.130
to bargain herself for the safety of the airbenders.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:20.500
I feel like if any of you have friends who
think Korra has been a selfish Avatar should

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.920
reference this as an example of Korra being
very not selfish. If you’re trying to argue

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:24.850
with them about it.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.420
Moving on to Number 9 - Tenzin is NOT Dead

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.890
This made me so happy. He’s such a guiding
force not just for Korra herself, but for

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:35.340
the series in general. Losing him would be
like losing your compass in the South Pole.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.630
The only person I feel could help guide Korra
and serve as a spiritual guide for the audience

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:43.400
would be Jinora or Zuko. Based on the way
the finale presented her I would say Jinora

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.070
is definitely the future.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:50.189
I’ll talk more about her as I work through
the list.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:52.360
Number 8 - The Doublecross

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.960
This was one of the most creative uses of
Waterbending I’ve seen. Book 2 pushed it

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.799
futher than I’d ever see it go before with
the water drills. But Ming Hua or Grey Delisle

00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:04.329
if you want to think about her that way. Pushed
the limits of waterbending the same way Zaheer

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:06.500
pushed airbending.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.790
Aside from crazy healing powers, I don’t
know what deep mythological abilities might

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:16.200
apply to water. We’ve already seen crazy
powerful bloodbending from Amon and Avatar

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.260
Last Airbender spent a lot of time showcasing
Katara’s special abilities.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.349
I guess that’s kind of what Ming Hua has
been for book 3. Like a super evil version

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:28.760
of Katara. We never really got to see Katara
in her prime as an adult so it would be hard

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:28.879
to say who’s the more gifted waterbender.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:31.190
And I don’t think Ming Hua would have had
the spirituality necessary for unlocking secret

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:31.629
abilities that went beyond subbending.

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:34.450
But Number 7 - Team Beifong Takes Out P’Li

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:39.540
One of the coolest takedowns all season. Metalbending
her armor around her head so the blast would

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.680
splatter her brains. Let me know if you think
there has been a more violent kill so far.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.110
The Earth Queen was like slow agony so I guess
you could say she had a more gruesome death.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:55.110
Which Zaheer confirmed when he pushed Korra’s
father off the cliff. I was happy he said

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:02.190
it out loud. So we can confirm no Earth Queen
in book 4.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:10.489
The whole fight scene was amazing and the
animation. There were a lot of specific animation

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:16.319
techniques I noticed that went way above and
beyond so I’ll try to mention them when

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:18.010
I talk about each of these big moments.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:24.080
Korra fighting while handcuffed as really
badass too.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.620
Number 6 - Zaheer Can Fly

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.640
This is where shit really got crazy. All of
the Guru Laghima stuff made sense, it was

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:34.230
a literal thing. Meaning the void was more
of a spiritual vacuum for emotion and earthly

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.540
attachment.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:42.239
It’s a big callback to Last Airbender’s
Guru Pathik who tried to get Aang to leave

00:03:42.239 --> 00:03:48.390
earthly attachment behind. That was all about
energy bending. But the chakras and Guru Laghima’s

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.879
teachings make me wonder if all bending has
a certain spiritual energy connected to it.

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:54.590
The way the show presents bending is as being
very separate. But when all the lessons start

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:59.260
to sound like the same lesson you start to
wonder. Like everyone is tending the same

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.140
garden, some just focus on different areas
of it based on their personality.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.290
That doesn’t really take the Lion Turtles
into account but let me know if you think

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:09.700
that Book 4 will build on all the new things
we’ve learned about Bending Science.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:14.680
Ooh, Bending Science, that actually sounds
like a class they should teach at Republic

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.440
City University.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:24.240
The Zaheer P’li moment was really bittersweet
and despite him being looney tunes, I think

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.639
his emotions for her were completely genuine.
He wasn’t manipulating her or anything.

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:35.000
Mike and Bryan just needed the scene to show
that once she was dead, Zaheer no longer had

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.960
any earthly tethers. Thus, he achieved flight.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.350
Did anyone else think he was walking on the
clouds when the camera panned down and showed

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:45.180
him, just for a sec it seemed like he would
walk away on the clouds.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.810
His flight animation was also really amazing,
I feel like they really capture the physics

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:51.540
of how an airbender would move through the
air.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:57.449
I think he was airbending himself. He wasn’t
airbending the air molecules around him. That’s

00:04:57.449 --> 00:05:01.970
just my interpretation though.

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:07.360
I know Jinora’s spirit projection is supposed
to be the sub form of airbending but did anyone

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:12.630
else think that Zaheer’s weightlessness
was actually what it was.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:16.259
I kind of think it’s like Earthbending having
two sub forms. Lava and Metal. So now Air

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:20.660
has two sub forms. Astral Projection and Flight.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:23.070
Number 5 - Bolin Lavabends

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.870
I think we all collectively felt he would
learn a subform this season. I actually thought

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.470
it would be metal bending. I would have liked
it better if Ghazan had taught him how to

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.460
do it but I guess there just wasn’t enough
time to give them that character arc.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:38.030
There was that awesome part during Book 1
where Tenzin taught Korra about Airbending,

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:43.380
it was so detailed in his description of where
you have to go emotionally in order to do

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.639
it. I feel like there’s still a lot about
Lavabending I still don’t understand because

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:47.820
we haven’t gotten that ‘lesson’ episode.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.080
It’s super rare, so I don’t see someone
explaining it to him in Book 4, unless it’s

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.919
someone in the fire nation. And yes, I do
think they’ll go back to the fire nation

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.630
in Book 4. Remember all the airbenders will
be nomadic.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:00.150
The only heartbreaking thing about Bolin’s
big moment was the destruction of the Northern

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:04.539
Air temple. It’s like watching someone destroy
a priceless piece of art. You just cringe

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:06.270
at the thought.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:13.270
Even though the air nomads will be roaming,
I still think the temple will be rebuilt eventually.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:17.419
But Number 4 - Zaheer Tries To Kill Korra
In the Avatar State

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:23.289
This was a huge callback to the Last Airbender
Book 2 finale. Especially with all the green

00:06:23.289 --> 00:06:28.370
crystals around. The outcome was essentially
the same. Aang went into a coma, effectively

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.819
rendering him inert until Book 3 and Korra
is severely disabled.

00:06:31.819 --> 00:06:35.819
When they said poison I didn’t realize it
was metal poison. But technically any kind

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:39.940
of metal in your body would poison you. So
I don’t think it’s really important what

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.169
kind of poison it was.

00:06:41.169 --> 00:06:44.509
The thing I really noticed aside from the
cave which was both beautiful and terrifying

00:06:44.509 --> 00:06:48.120
was the Dai Li agents. The Red Lotus has members
inside the Dai Li. Making me wonder if The

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:54.210
Red Lotus guided a lot of the Earth Queen’s
mistakes. Like counseled her to make decisions

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.720
that would set the Earth Kingdom on the path
to destruction.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.319
I’ll talk more about that in my book 4 predictions
video.

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:02.210
I had thought before this all went down that
part of this idea of Entering the Void might

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.360
be some sort of journey into death. Which
is naturally me just overthinking things.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.930
Who else flipped a little when they saw the
animation on Korra, especially her face as

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:11.280
the poison started to take effect. I love
the way Studio Mir pushed Korra in a more

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:16.380
Anime direction this year. It makes me feel
like we’ll see more of the same in Book

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.000
4.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.810
Mike and Bryan already said that another studio
was helping finish book 4, but Studio Mir

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:25.069
is animating pretty much every episode. They’re
just getting a little bump to get everything

00:07:25.069 --> 00:07:27.319
out by next year.

00:07:27.319 --> 00:07:30.810
Into top 3 now, Number 3 - Jinora and the
Airbenders rescue Korra

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:34.180
One of the coolest uses of Bending all season.
It reminds you that there are still a lot

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.099
of creative innovations in bending that we
have not seen yet. I’m really interested

00:07:38.099 --> 00:07:43.210
to see if we see some unusual firebending
in the fire nation in book 4.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:50.210
I felt like this was a big callback to Jinora
rescuing Raava in the book 2 finale. Which

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:56.680
makes me feel like Mike and Bryan are positioning
her for a spin off comic or at least presenting

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:01.720
her as the future of the Avatar Universe when
they stop telling Korra driven stories.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:05.539
Like the way Zuko became the central figure
in the Search comic. I feel like there’s

00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:07.849
potential for a Jinora story in the comics.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:09.949
On to Number 2 - Korra vs Zaheer

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:12.169
This is Korra in auto Avatar State mode. She
reminded me a lot of Aang back in Book 1 when

00:08:12.169 --> 00:08:16.680
he first learned that the Air Nation had been
massacred and he flipped out so hardcore that

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:21.449
he went into the avatar state and almost no
one could talk him down.

00:08:21.449 --> 00:08:26.099
Since then both Last Airbender and Korra have
done a good job of explaining the postives

00:08:26.099 --> 00:08:29.849
and negatives of being in the avatar state.
It’s so powerful that your conscious mind

00:08:29.849 --> 00:08:33.120
gets suppressed a little and you literally
become a force of nature. So if you’re not

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:36.919
highly trained the potential for collateral
damage is really high. And you become super

00:08:36.919 --> 00:08:37.839
vulnerable.
I don’t totally buy into the logic that

00:08:37.839 --> 00:08:38.690
dying in the avatar state ends the cycle.
I think it’s just a story device that keeps

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:39.430
the Avatar from becoming an unkillable hero.
In order for there to be dramatic tension,

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:40.896
a writing perspective.

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:46.750
think about as they fought while flying after
each other. I loved the twist that Korra was

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:50.420
using fire bending to fly like Ozai and Zaheer
used airbending like Aang.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:53.640
Just another twist on a classic. And then
just to call it back to Aang again, when Beifong

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.380
earthbended Zaheer’s prison. It was just
like the scene where Aang took Yakone’s

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:57.899
bending.

00:08:57.899 --> 00:09:04.899
And my favorite moment - Jinora’s Ceremony

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:12.529
I will freely admit to crying a little. This
was probably the best callback to Last Airbender

00:09:12.529 --> 00:09:17.180
or at least my favorite. When Aang got his
ceremony at the end of Book 1. He was accepting

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:22.730
his role as the Avatar and Jinora was accepting
her role as the new spiritual leader of the

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:23.630
Air Nation.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:28.190
Just to clarify, I think Tenzin was explaining
that Jinora would be in charge and he would

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:32.380
just be counseling her. This is a huge payoff
to the father daughter relationship story

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:36.560
they had this year. It’s him acknowledging
her abilities and maturity.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:40.240
I feel like this season would be a great story
arc for any of you girls out there to watch

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.970
with your dad’s. Especially if you want
to get your parents into Avatar.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.330
I have a lot of thoughts about Book 4 which
I’ll mostly save for my predictions video.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:50.029
I’ll try and post that tonight while everything
is fresh in our heads.

00:09:50.029 --> 00:09:54.100
But let me know what your favorite moments
were and let me know what your first reaction

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.180
was after finishing the episodes.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:10:01.120
I think the first thing I did was post a picture
of Aang crying. That was my immediate reaction,

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.740
lots of crying.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:08.910
Overall, both finale episodes were a solid
A plus, I loved the way they altered all the

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:12.019
characters, I thought the narrative was a
lot more engaging and cohesive than previous

00:10:12.019 --> 00:10:17.320
seasons and they continued to push the boundaries
of animation on the series.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:21.310
Just to talk about that a little more. Mike
and Bryan did this podcast recently which

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:28.310
I’ll add a link in the description too.
It was brilliant. But amongst many things,

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:33.600
they explained the way they like to run their
shows. Letting animators be animators, based

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.959
on the style they want for Korra.

00:10:35.959 --> 00:10:40.560
For example, on most Animated shows in the
united states. The overseas animators are

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.990
very limited to what they can do. Like they’re
not allowed to be real animators, they have

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.269
to adhere to such strict rules for drawing
scenes.

00:10:46.269 --> 00:10:50.250
But Mike and Bryan with Korra have tried to
find a way to allow some creativity back into

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:55.130
the process. Mostly by finding animators that
could pull off what they had in mind and allowing

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.800
new ideas in during the animation process.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:01.140
I think that’s why the Beifong flashbacks
looked so amazing, they were a totally different

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:05.779
animation style than normal korra episodes.
And you wouldn’t see that on a typical animated

00:11:05.779 --> 00:11:09.490
children’s show. It’s just a good example
of the attention they give to the creative

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:13.550
process and I think it’s one of the best
things about the Avatar series.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:17.279
Most of the feelings I have about the series
right now are optimistic. They were pretty

00:11:17.279 --> 00:11:22.019
clear that after Book 4 they would not be
animating another avatar series. They’d

00:11:22.019 --> 00:11:25.060
be doing something, just not Avatar. It’s
all in that podcast.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:25.640
Speaking of which, they disseminated so much
information that I’m going to do another

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:32.640
bonus video in the next couple of days that’s
my Mike and Bryan Top 10 Moments. It’s all

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:38.540
cool behind the scenes stuff. They even explain
what happened with the Avatar Movie from M

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:38.920
Night.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:42.170
The most interesting thought that I’ll leave
you guys with is that Mike and Bryan said

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:45.630
because the animation process takes so long,
they’ve already wrapped up everything that

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:49.700
you have big questions about. Any hanging
plotline or character you feel got dropped.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:53.470
Like Azula for instance. They have all addressed
in future Book 4 stories.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:57.440
So leave book 3 knowing that all of your questions
will be addressed in those episodes.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.920
Like I said though, I’ll explain what I
think is going on in my predictions video.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:01.769
I’ll try to post that tonight.

00:12:01.769 --> 00:12:03.940
I know there’s a bunch of Doctor Who stuff
I’m working on too so I’ll try to get

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:05.850
it all out as fast as possible.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:09.980
Right now click here for Book 4 predictions.
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:10.170
it.

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:13.779
And click here for my next Korra Q&amp;A. I might
not be able to post that till Monday.

00:12:13.779 --> 00:12:18.360
Thanks for watching, I’ll still be crying
with you guys tonight. Let’s all go hug

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:21.560
our sky bison.

